0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
70.8661417322834666 742.9608661417322537 Td
(The XIRR is defined as the discount rate r that satisfies the equation: NPV\(r\) = Sum\(C_i / \(1 + r\)^\(\(d_i - d_0\)/365\)\) = 0,) Tj
T* (where C_i represents cashflows and d_i represents transaction dates. The Newton-Raphson iteration updates r via:) Tj
T* (r_{k+1} = r_k - NPV\(r_k\) / NPV'\(r_k\):) Tj
