/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.118 0.161 0.231 rg
70.8661417322834666 571.3476771653542983 Td
(Let g\(r\) = r - f\(r\)/f'\(r\). By Taylor's theorem, expanding around the root r*: f\(r*\) = 0. Expanding f\(r_k\) and f'\(r_k\) around r*) Tj
T* (shows that the error e_{k+1} = r_{k+1} - r* satisfies: e_{k+1} approx \(f''\(r*\) / \(2 f'\(r*\)\)\) * e_k^2. Because the error at step) Tj
T* (k+1 is proportional to the square of the error at step k, the Newton-Raphson algorithm exhibits quadratic convergence,) Tj
T* (doubling the number of accurate decimal digits in each iteration once in proximity to the root. For typical 5-year retail) Tj
T* (investment cashflows, exact convergence is achieved within 6 to 8 iterations.) Tj
ET
